35,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,"The budget is down a quarter. Fitting out is now charged to development, not estates.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Shion,,The call-back trial reduced readmissions by a fifth. But the booking system misses unbooked work.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Midori,,Nine nursing posts are empty. Agency cover is rising. Therapy staff are leaving for the city.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Kenji,,Outpatient rooms book out by mid-morning. The car park fills before eleven. Shuttle covers only four villages.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Shizue,,The joint clinic closed in a year. Neither department wanted the rota. Data agreements take fourteen months.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Midori, if agency cover is rising, any new program will drain the budget further.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Shion,,"@Jonathan, the readmission data proves home visits work. But we need to track them properly.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Midori,,"@Shion, home visits need nurses. We have nine vacancies. Who will do the visiting?","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Shion, if the booking system misses unbooked work, how do we prove the program works?","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Shizue,,"@Midori, the joint clinic failed because of shared responsibility. We must avoid that trap.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Jonathan,,"@Shizue, the data agreement delay is a major risk for any external coordination.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Shion,,"@Kenji, the booking system is a blind spot. We need a program that fits existing slots.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Midori,,"@Shion, the therapy staffing review shows physios are leaving. A rehab unit is risky.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Kenji,,"@Midori, the car park is full. A day unit will make the traffic worse.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Shizue,,"@Jonathan, the budget cut means we cannot afford expensive fitting out. We need a lean option.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Jonathan,,We need a program that fits the budget and the staffing reality.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Shion,,The readmission data is strong. Home follow-up seems the most evidence-based.,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Midori,,The midwifery rota has slack. That might be a good place to start.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Kenji,,Home visits avoid the car park and room issues. That is a big plus.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Shizue,,We must avoid joint management. A single department should own the program.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
